Falsifies `grant_plan::parsing::verification::every_token_is_a_nonempty_slice_of_the_line_in_order`.

The defect: the tokenizer stores a token even when the scan stopped where it started, so trailing whitespace yields an empty token.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(!t.is_empty())`.

diff --git a/src/parsing.rs b/src/parsing.rs
--- a/src/parsing.rs
+++ b/src/parsing.rs
@@ -40,10 +40,8 @@
             c.step(line[i]);
             i += 1;
         }
-        if i > start {
-            out[n] = &line[start..i];
-            n += 1;
-        }
+        out[n] = &line[start..i];
+        n += 1;
     }
     (&out[..n], &line[i..])
 }
